A||||4||GT Bastard||Swapping petal assemblies from auto to man...||||5||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||05-06-2000||04:25 PM||||A couple of people have said that swapping petal assemblies from auto to manual is a royal pain.  Why is this?  That's really the only part of the swap that bugs me now.  The rest seems doable.  I've heard that part of the steering column needs to be dissasembled to accomplish this, but why?  thanks for the info guys.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodney||05-07-2000||07:41 AM||||It is not that hard if you know the trick! Take a sawzall and cut the old pedal bracket in half when it is still boltd in place. Then it easily comes out. On the new bracket cut the bolts(studs) off and drill out the heads. Install it with new bolts and nuts. Slides right into place then. Easy!||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||05-07-2000||05:03 PM||||The only problem is not having any power in my garage.... poop.  Is it a real pain to do it the other way?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan86gt3.8||05-08-2000||10:49 AM||||when I did manual to auto pedals it was fiarly easy, but the steering column was out so I don't know if its in the way when its in or what.  Also the bolts are kinda hard to get to cause they are right behind the brake booster.  Other than the bolts being a pain to get too its fiarly easy||||reg||1
Z||000004||coyote||05-10-2000||12:59 PM||||It is not that big of a deal!! you will have to drop the steering column. you just need to be careful , there is a harness that runs along the pedal bracket that will give you a little grief, but other than that just do it. takes me about 30 mins.<P>Good luck||||reg||1
